{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLMidiDevice","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLMidiDeviceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"midiInstrument","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLMidiInstrument","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLMidiInstrumentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLScorePart\/Group2-swift.struct\/init(midiDevice:midiInstrument:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLScorePart/Group2-swift.struct/init(midiDevice:midiInstrument:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLScorePart.Group2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"midiDevice","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLMidiDeviceV","text":"MXLMidiDevice","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"midiInstrument","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLMidiInstrumentV","text":"MXLMidiInstrument","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"title":"init(midiDevice:midiInstrument:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLScorePart\/Group2-swift.struct\/init(midiDevice:midiInstrument:)","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlscorepart\/group2-swift.struct\/init(mididevice:midiinstrument:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLScorePart":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The score-part type collects part-wide information for each part in a score. Often, each MusicXML part"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corresponds to a track in a Standard MIDI Format 1 file. In this case, the midi-device element is used to make"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a MIDI device or port assignment for the given track or specific MIDI instruments. Initial midi-instrument"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"assignments may be made here as well. The score-instrument elements are used when there are multiple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"instruments per track.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLScorePart"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLScorePart"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlscorepart","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLScorePart","title":"MXLScorePart"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMidiInstrument":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The midi-instrument type defines MIDI 1.0 instrument playback. The midi-instrument element can be a part of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"either the score-instrument element at the start of a part, or the sound element within a part. The id","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute refers to the score-instrument affected by the change.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLMidiInstrument","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMidiInstrument","title":"MXLMidiInstrument","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmidiinstrument","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLMidiInstrument","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLScorePart/Group2-swift.struct":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLScorePart\/Group2-swift.struct","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlscorepart\/group2-swift.struct","abstract":[{"text":"A single MIDI device and instrument assignment for a score-part.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MXLScorePart.Group2","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Group2"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Group2"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMidiDevice":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMidiDevice"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMidiDevice"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmididevice","role":"symbol","title":"MXLMidiDevice","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMidiDevice","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The midi-device type corresponds to the DeviceName meta event in Standard MIDI Files. The optional port"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"attribute is a number from 1 to 16 that can be used with the unofficial MIDI 1.0 port (or cable) meta event.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Unlike the DeviceName meta event, there can be multiple midi-device elements per MusicXML part. The optional","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"id attribute refers to the score-instrument assigned to this device. If missing, the device assignment affects","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"all score-instrument elements in the score-part."}]}}}